    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0218" n="136" xml:id="pg136"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Harvey</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 178.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 13, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of August 8, No. 353, has
                    been received. The course pursued by you on receiving my instruction enclosing
                    the President’s proclamation in regard to the harboring or giving of hospitality
                    to insurgent cruisers and the proceedings of the Portuguese government in
                    relation thereto were doubtless sufficient, and they are satisfactory. It is for
                    the government of Portugal to decide whether it desires to be undemonstrative in
                    the matter. We ask nothing.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
